{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 0, "start_seconds": 0.0, "end_seconds": 4.639999866485596, "text": "Try this. Put on a latex glove and then put your hand into ice-cold water.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 1, "start_seconds": 4.639999866485596, "end_seconds": 6.800000190734863, "text": "You'll notice it still feels wet.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 2, "start_seconds": 7.760000228881836, "end_seconds": 12.5600004196167, "text": "But that's strange because the glove is impermeable to water, but it still feels wet.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 3, "start_seconds": 12.5600004196167, "end_seconds": 15.760000228881836, "text": "That's because we actually don't have a way to directly measure wetness.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 4, "start_seconds": 15.760000228881836, "end_seconds": 18.399999618530273, "text": "Instead, we use temperature changes as a proxy.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 5, "start_seconds": 18.399999618530273, "end_seconds": 22.399999618530273, "text": "And that works most of the time because water conducts heat 23 times faster than air.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 6, "start_seconds": 22.399999618530273, "end_seconds": 25.360000610351562, "text": "So your skin touches water, it pulls away heat,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 7, "start_seconds": 25.360000610351562, "end_seconds": 28.31999969482422, "text": "and your brain interprets that loss of heat as wet.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 8, "start_seconds": 28.31999969482422, "end_seconds": 32.560001373291016, "text": "And that's why 15 degree water feels a lot colder than 15 degree air.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 9, "start_seconds": 32.560001373291016, "end_seconds": 36.560001373291016, "text": "As long as it kept us dry enough to survive and did not die of hypothermia,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 10, "start_seconds": 36.560001373291016, "end_seconds": 38.15999984741211, "text": "this heat trick was good enough.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 11, "start_seconds": 38.15999984741211, "end_seconds": 39.84000015258789, "text": "But not so for insects.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 12, "start_seconds": 39.84000015258789, "end_seconds": 42.47999954223633, "text": "At these scales, water is dangerously sticky.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 13, "start_seconds": 42.47999954223633, "end_seconds": 45.52000045776367, "text": "So many insects adapted these microscopic hairs,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 14, "start_seconds": 45.52000045776367, "end_seconds": 47.439998626708984, "text": "which deform in the presence of moisture.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 15, "start_seconds": 47.439998626708984, "end_seconds": 49.20000076293945, "text": "And this let them detect water directly.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 16, "start_seconds": 49.20000076293945, "end_seconds": 51.36000061035156, "text": "So flies actually know something we don't.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "DJ_5_JS9_Rs", "segment_index": 17, "start_seconds": 51.36000061035156, "end_seconds": 53.119998931884766, "text": "Whether water really is wet.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
